1 · Recap - the class you built yesterday
Yesterday you built Value: a number that also remembers how it was computed. Every time you combine Values with +, *, **, exp, log, or relu, the result stores three things:

data - the actual number;
_children - the Values it was built from;
_local_grads - the local derivative of the result with respect to each child.

That last one is the key idea. For c = a * b, the local derivatives are \(\partial c/\partial a = b\) and \(\partial c/\partial b = a\), so the multiply op stores (b.data, a.data). Each node is a little packet that knows its own one-step calculus.
